Third-party software in SEMQ SDK distributions

The npm package @semq/sdk contains a WebAssembly module and its JavaScript
loader, both built with the Emscripten toolchain. They include compiled
portions of the components listed below. The Python wheels, the Rust crates
and the Go module contain no third-party code.

Components:

  * Emscripten: JavaScript loader, C library additions and memory routines.
    MIT License or University of Illinois/NCSA Open Source License.
    https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten

  * musl libc: C library routines.
    MIT License.
    https://musl.libc.org

  * dlmalloc, by Doug Lea: memory allocator.
    Public domain (CC0 1.0).
    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

  * LLVM compiler-rt builtins: compiler support routines.
    Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. Under those exceptions, portions
    embedded in compiled object code may be redistributed without the
    attribution conditions of sections 4(a), 4(b) and 4(d).
    https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

